  "notes": [
    "One entry per SaaS a company may use. key is stable: company allowlists, reports and the console name a SaaS by it.",
    "web: host patterns. 'app.example.com' matches that host and its subdomains; '*.example.com' matches subdomains only. webExclude lists hosts that never count (the vendor's marketing, help and status sites). When two entries match a host, the longer pattern wins.",
    "macos: bundle ids of the desktop client, exact. windows: a case-insensitive regular expression on the program's name in Installed apps. windowsStore: one on the Microsoft Store package family name.",
    "research: the Sanka Research DNS rule family (sanka-api monitor_companies/signatures.json) for the same product, so a company's outside-in and on-PC results join.",
    "migrate: the Sanka migration page, https://sanka.com/migrate/<migrate>/. connector: the sanka-api migration connector (provider id) that moves its data, when one exists."
  ],
